each opinion.1. What current diagnosis or diagnoses and clinically significant findings are supported by the supplied evidence?2. What medical relationship, if any, is supported or not supported by the evidence for the claim issue under review?3. If causation and aggravation are medically applicable to the requested review, address each separately.4. Identify the specific records and medical or scientific literature relied upon, explain the medical rationale, and discuss material evidence that weighs against the opinion.Appendix A — Medical EvidenceContains clinical notes, diagnostic reports, treatment records, and related medical evidence.No medical evidence is included in this package.Appendix B — Medical Opinion EvidenceContains medical opinion and nexus evidence supplied for review.No medical opinion evidence is included in this package.Appendix C — Service RecordsContains relevant military service and service-treatment evidence.No service records are included in this package.Appendix D — Lay EvidenceContains statements and observations from the veteran and other lay witnesses.No lay evidence is included in this package.Appendix E — Adjudicative RecordsContains relevant VA decisions and adjudicative records.No adjudicative records are included in this package.Appendix F — Medical / Scientific LiteratureContains the medical/scientific literature supplied for review.No medical/scientific literature is included in this package.Additional EvidenceSource EvidenceBeforeAfter Beyond
